:[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T15:21:03-07:00","id":1262004,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the Venombites, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T15:36:34-07:00","id":1262007,"title":"","content":"Oni have always been a favourite of mine. I'd also say Skitterskulk, Venombite, Tunnelgrub, and Gremling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T16:34:55-07:00","id":1262016,"title":"","content":"My favorites were Skitterskulk, Venombite, Water-Dweller and Corpsegrinder. Of the mythical ones, I'm fond of Pishacha and Gremlin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T16:43:20-07:00","id":1262018,"title":"","content":"Coldscale, Riddleseeker, Venombite, Romancer, Corpsegrinders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T17:25:43-07:00","id":1262023,"title":"","content":"Truefriend, Antiquarian, Manikin, Treasured, Farwalker, Bloodbrute, Witchtooth, Chirurgeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T19:13:07-07:00","id":1262035,"title":"","content":"I was always a big fan of Stonebones, Render, Gremlin, Witchtooth, Lurkglider, Gargantuan, Chirurgeon, Bloodbrute, Draconic, Succubus, and Brewer. Really, I loved almost all of them, but those are a few I used an awful lot in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 10-21-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T19:29:33-07:00","id":1262037,"title":"","content":"Draconics and Stonebones/Earthbones/Metalflesh. I love my elemental tanks, but we probably only need one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T02:36:01-07:00","id":1262093,"title":"","content":"Muse, Drudge, Oracle, Whisperwisp, Manikin and Chimera. Can't wait to see them pop out in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T03:09:04-07:00","id":1262101,"title":"","content":"Coldscales, Skitterskulk, Manikin, Draconic, Cyclopean, Witchtooth, Drudge, Gameplayer, Oracle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T09:40:29-07:00","id":1262170,"title":"","content":"Gosh, I love so many of them...but I'll try and keep it narrowed down!<br /> <br /> Whisperwisp and/or Cleareyes \u2013\u2013 I love to play characters that are finders and potential spies.<br /> <br /> Chirurgeon \u2013\u2013 In my limited experience as a GM, players don't pick up Medicine dots until they learn how potent a good doctor can be. Chirurgeon seems like a fun and perfect way to make a potential player consider investing in Medicine \u2013\u2013 and also a good kith to have around as a GM.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A friend without an account here begged me to add: Shadowsoul! (He loves the aesthetic and feel of that kith. It also has a special place in my heart, admittedly\u2013\u2013it's a sort of &quot;edgy&quot; kith that I'd be so afraid to play when I was younger, but as an adult, I say: who's going to stop me?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":22860,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22860-miirik","user":"Miirik","date":". 11-11-2018, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22860-miirik","name":"Miirik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T09:47:24-07:00","id":1262175,"title":"","content":"Airtouched, Antiquarian, Chimera, Chirurgeon, and Coldscale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T12:33:23-07:00","id":1262201,"title":"","content":"Big question. <br /> I suppose I'll limit it to 5 (but in no particular order, I loved these either Playing or seeing played)<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Coldscale (mostly the types of chars made when the idea was &quot;lizardlike&quot; were all great chars.)</li> <li>Gravewight (I've seen two of these and, while not inherent to the kith, both played like fantastic sardonic wit haunted chars)</li> <li>Manikin (great drama for these characters and all who knew them. Their humanity wittled down more than some.)</li> <li>Draconic (interestingly, it wasn't the martial ability or background that tied all of these chars together as the same kith. It was this propensity for a fatalistic world view. Not sure if the kith did that or if each player just slipped into that with the background the Char had.)</li> <li>Oni</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T17:44:02-07:00","id":1262257,"title":"","content":"I have always favored the Wizened kiths such Smith, Artist, Soldier, Brewer, and Chirugeon. For the other seemings, I would go with Truefriend, Airtouched, Venombite, Tunnelgrub, Treasured, Farwalker, Renderer, Gremlin, and Hunterheart. Also Manikin and Chatelaine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","user":"Extant Reality","date":". 10-26-2018, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:32:23-07:00","id":1262413,"title":"","content":"I think the that ones that I miss the most are as follows:<br /> <br /> Flowering - My favourite Fairest 1E kith. Loved the idea of flower fairies with enchanting perfume.<br /> Treasured - Bling bling changelings with added durability. Much flash. <br /> Brewer - I love the brewer, but i can see why they weren't included as they are super problematic. A whole kith whose central power is the ability to drug people's drinks? yeah, not flying anymore.<br /> Manikin - I have no idea why this wasn't included.<br /> Oracle - I guess I can see the point of this being excluded, as all changelings are potential oracles thanks to contracts and onieromancy.<br /> Woodwalker - I just like 'em. The ability to gain nutritional benefit from any found plant is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T14:57:33-07:00","id":1262419,"title":"","content":"For me it would be<br /> <br /> 1. Gameplayer - Wizened <br /> 2. Razorhand - Darkling<br /> 3. Weisse Frau - Fairest<br /> 4. Gargantuan- Ogre<br /> 5. Chimera - Beast<br /> 6. Blightbent - Elemental","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T16:07:35-07:00","id":1262430,"title":"","content":"So many choices, also going to trim down to 5:<br /> <br /> Antiquarian, Cleareyes, Coldscale, Gameplayer, and Witchtooth<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> A bit of an amendment after thoughts. I'd consider Cyclopean and Prismatic included in this because they overlap with Cleareyes and Coldscale respectively, just for different Seemings (and slightly different mechanics). With 2e separating them out, we don't need two &quot;awesome perception&quot; Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-23-2018, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T17:50:59-07:00","id":1262444,"title":"","content":"Oooh soo many good ones, i will try to put one from each seeming<br /> -Beast: Windwing<br /> -Darkling: Moonborn<br /> -Elemental: Manikin<br /> -Fairest: Draconic<br /> -Ogre: WitchTooth<br /> -Wizened: Brewer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","user":"Queer Snake","date":". 10-23-2018, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-23T20:55:38-07:00","id":1262466,"title":"","content":"My favorites were<br /> Beast: Venombite<br /> Darkling: Razorhand<br /> Fairest: Draconic<br /> Ogre: Ifreet<br /> Wizened: Soldier","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T00:39:02-07:00","id":1262483,"title":"","content":"If I had to pick, my top choice would be Riddleseeker, followed closely by Whisperwisp and Succubus. I Also really like Gravewights for Mixed games (say a Geister, a Moros Mage, a Gravewight, a Begotten, and a Nepri. Gives them a good mix, and gives them a direction: The Underworld). Also, though I know its not a 1E Kith, I really liked the concept of the Greys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 10-24-2018, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T03:22:42-07:00","id":1262490,"title":"","content":"Airtouched <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-24T14:46:13-07:00","id":1262588,"title":"","content":"Going through the list, we've got<br /> <br /> *checks*<br /> <br /> Beast: First favorites are Coyote and Windwing, followed by Truefriend, Riddleseeker, and Hunterheart.<br /> Darklings: First favorites are Nightsinger and Illes, followed by Palewraith, Mirrorskin, and Razorhand.<br /> Elementals: First favorites are the Ask-wee-da-eed and the Fireheart, followed by Waterborn, Woodblood, and Levinquick.<br /> Fairest: First favorites are the Flamesiren and Weiss Frau, followed by the Shadowsoul, Dancer, and Larcenist.<br /> Ogres: First favorites are the Witchtooth and Troll, followed by the Gristlegrinder, Bloodbrute, and Farwalker.<br /> Wizened: First Favorites are....Christ, really the Oracle, Author, Brewer, and Gameplayer, followed by the Fatemaker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T18:09:37-07:00","id":1262776,"title":"","content":"Every CtL group I\u2019ve ever been in has had at least one Hunterheart for the unarmed lethal.<br /> <br /> General personal favorites: Truefriend, Antiquarian, Gravewright, Razorhand, Moonborn, Manikin, Mirrorskin, Gristlegrinder, Chirurgeon. Can you tell I really liked Darklings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:50:16-07:00","id":1263375,"title":"","content":"Man I have so many I love, Levinquick because I am a sucker for electricity powers, Manikin, Palewraith, Draconic.<br /> <br /> While not a 1ed one, something that had caught my eye and I loved for making my own twisted interpretation of the Crystal Gems, The Jeweleyes Kith from the previews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24753-phantoms-heart","name":"Phantoms-Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theo